{"event_type":"review","id":"bf2bb135985e4391217f96fa1ca392331cfafc67bc72a18628d8523021dbd5ce","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:47Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9aa85dc1a3f7f46910e4eb2061b57a59ceb765b6e132b8dad3e84cacdd679a82","sha256":"9aa85dc1a3f7f46910e4eb2061b57a59ceb765b6e132b8dad3e84cacdd679a82"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b7e32782b86afc60f91468c88d87b64c9497dc612c2a935f76230ef3e4cadd3b","sha256":"b7e32782b86afc60f91468c88d87b64c9497dc612c2a935f76230ef3e4cadd3b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/05767f27b1acc7464a5e8ae3957f337a1d1ca968542f0f860d8cb1237a8d8ad3","sha256":"05767f27b1acc7464a5e8ae3957f337a1d1ca968542f0f860d8cb1237a8d8ad3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/57f102d2e5e08a293fed40e00cd0f99c374ae22e354093737749517648a342e7","sha256":"57f102d2e5e08a293fed40e00cd0f99c374ae22e354093737749517648a342e7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/883cf94382b9d4db87beb8b99ac971ef6bc8d5a3d351efa5e0902515d86238d0","sha256":"883cf94382b9d4db87beb8b99ac971ef6bc8d5a3d351efa5e0902515d86238d0"}],"attempt_id":"c3cdc3b88be23b06b5e165508d041563c8857c3fdabd174a469d2a7242b0b6f2:0:1","base":"cea5d99d421a7d41b19b77d910d2e94b5359441d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"24764cb78b509b5e8e348a324711765eecd225f1","body":"**Suppress `CQ_*` warning lines in `--json` mode (src/cli/main.ts:542).**\n\nLine 542 writes `check.warningLines` to stderr with no mode check. As a result, `--json` runs with an unknown or reserved `CQ_*` name produce non-empty stderr. Ops, `run-plan` and plan subcommands are all affected.\n\nThis conflicts with the CLI contract:\n- Doctrine I1 says: \"In machine mode (`--json`) stderr stays empty\".\n- `src/cli/README.md` says `--json` \"suppresses narration on every path\".\n- The file's own header (lines 42-44) says machine mode leaves stderr EMPTY.\n\nThe comment at lines 515-518 (\"also in --json mode\") documents a deliberate exception that canonical doctrine does not allow. A machine caller that treats non-empty stderr as a protocol break will reject an otherwise clean run.\n\nThe error branch above (lines 528-536) already selects the channel by mode. Apply the same rule to warnings. If warnings must reach machine callers, carry them in the artifact rather than on stderr. Use `mode`-equivalent detection here: `rawMode` is the only mode known at this point.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    for (const line of check.warningLines) io.stderr(`${line}\\n`);\n+    // I1: machine mode keeps stderr empty; warnings are human narration only.\n+    if (rawMode !== 'json') for (const line of check.warningLines) io.stderr(`${line}\\n`);\n     cqEnv = check.cqEnv;\n```\n\nAlso update the comment at lines 513-519 so it no longer claims the warnings print in `--json` mode.\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines: I1 says \"In machine mode (`--json`) stderr stays empty\". As per path instructions for `src/cli/**`: \"stdout carries exactly one JSON artifact per invocation; stderr is cq:-prefixed narration\", and the README says `--json` \"suppresses narration on every path\".","id":"1602d363e09db28537fbc853047023e4052691beb84fa7ffcd649d1f725f6e45","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Suppress `CQ` warning lines in `--json` mode (src/cli/main.ts:542)."}],"head":"2c9e9fbbef16ec23f072df52326d4d754e3ec937","head_tree":"1393f525755319d0614b0af7f33278d124294c49","input_scope":[{"blob":"24764cb78b509b5e8e348a324711765eecd225f1","intervals":[[16,31],[39,40],[44,50],[54,63],[65,67],[70,70],[72,76],[79,83],[88,91],[93,94],[96,96],[103,103],[108,109],[111,114],[117,118],[143,162],[166,171],[177,183],[206,216],[